## PATH A — Complex Questions (skip structure, maximize compute time)

You have 10 minutes. Every second counts. Search the corpus immediately, extract all needed data points into Python, compute the answer, verify once, write it.

**Domain traps:**
- Fiscal year ends June 30 (pre-1976) or Sep 30 (post-1976). Calendar year ends Dec 31.
- Data for period X → bulletins AFTER period X.
- "Public debt" ≠ "total gross federal debt." Verify row labels exactly.
- If question says "total" and you found a line item, look for the parent row.

Go. Search → Extract → Compute → Verify → Write `/app/answer.txt`.

